hw/sh4: ze0 SSI audio: PCM sink for WaveSSI1/2 over HPB-DMAC (TODO M8.H46).

EU2011 build B maps wavessi1/2's PCM path at phys 0xffe00000 (SSI) with an
area-7 alias at 0x1fe00000; the nk.exe OAL interrupt table attributes
SYSINTR 0x24 (WaveSSI1) to HPB-DMAC channels 11 (INTEVT 0xcc0, ISR
0x8803e8e4) and 12 (0xda0, 0x8803e98c), and SYSINTR 0x25 (WaveSSI2) to
channel 13 (0xdc0, 0x8803ea14).  The ISRs test DINTSR0 bits 11/12/13.

hw/sh4/ze0_ssi.c: a register file for the three SSI blocks (0x10000 stride)
so the driver's mapping and reset writes land in memory, plus a QEMU
audiodev voice.  When an HPB-DMAC channel is armed with DDAR inside the
SSI block, ze0_hpbdmac_run_ssi() moves the buffer into the voice; a
machine option ssi-audio=ID binds -audiodev wav.  ssi-selftest=N is an
explicit positive control that pushes N bytes of PCM through the same
DMA path (off by default; not guest playback).

Base: QEMU 11.1.3 with the earlier patches of this directory, in sorted
order (sorts after ze0-h01).  Evidence: EXP-2026-11-22-M8.H46-ssi-audio.
